\details{
\subsection{Composition generation model}{

Let \strong{q} be the OM-predicted composition vector (length \code{nBin}, sums to 1)
for a given simulation, year, and fleet. The observation error model
proceeds as follows:

\strong{Step 1 — Base concentration vector}

\deqn{\alpha = \mathrm{ESS} \times \mathbf{q}}

\strong{Step 2 — Apply log-concentration offset (if \code{Shift} non-\code{NULL})}

\deqn{\alpha_b' = \alpha_b \times \exp(\mathrm{Shift}[\mathrm{sim}, \mathrm{year}, b])}

When \code{Shift} is \code{NULL}, \eqn{\alpha' = \alpha}.

\strong{Step 3 — Dirichlet draw}

\deqn{\mathbf{p}^* \sim \mathrm{Dirichlet}(\alpha' / \mathrm{Theta})}

where \code{Theta} \eqn{\in (0, 1]} controls overdispersion. \code{Theta = 1}
recovers the standard Dirichlet with concentration \eqn{\alpha'}.
Smaller values of \code{Theta} shrink the total concentration and increase
variance.

\strong{Step 4 — Multinomial draw}

\deqn{\mathrm{obs} \sim \mathrm{Multinomial}(\mathrm{SampleSize},\, \mathbf{p}^*)}
}

\subsection{Conditioning mode}{

When real composition data are supplied via \code{OM@Data}, \code{\link[=ConditionObs_Comp]{ConditionObs_Comp()}}
compares observed compositions with OM-predicted compositions across the
historical years specified in \code{Years}, and populates \code{Shift} (mean per-bin
log-concentration residual) as well as estimating an appropriate \code{ESS} and
\code{Theta}. Users should not set these slots manually when conditioning on
real data.

Note: when observed compositions differ substantially from OM-predicted
compositions (e.g. a length distribution shifted far left or right, or
with markedly different spread), the resulting \code{Shift} values will be
large. This is treated as observation error rather than model
mis-specification — an assumption that should be evaluated carefully. See
the technical manual for a full discussion.
}

